    <code code="18776-5" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Plan of care note"/>
    <title>Plan of Treatment</title>
    <text><list><item>Medication: continued without change, Acetaminophen 500 mg oral tablet, two tablets by mouth as needed for headache, no more than 2 days a week [S]</item><item>Medication: stopped, Candesartan 8 mg oral tablet, one tablet by mouth daily [S]</item><item>Medication: started, Candesartan 16 mg oral tablet, one tablet by mouth daily [S]</item><item>Medication: started, Modafinil 100 mg oral tablet, one tablet by mouth each morning [S]</item><item>Goal: Stop daily over-the-counter analgesics and limit acute headache medicine to no more than 2 days a week. Outcome by 1897-05-18: No ibuprofen since the first visit; acetaminophen about once a week [S]</item><item>Goal: Cut headache days by at least half by the three-month review. In progress; target 1897-08-17 [S]</item><item>Goal: Reduce daytime sleep attacks and lower the PROMIS sleep-related impairment T-score below 60. In progress; target 1897-08-17 [S]</item><item>Goal: Establish whether the spells are epileptic before considering antiseizure medicine. Outcome by 1897-05-18: Typical spells captured on ambulatory EEG were sleep onset; no antiseizure medicine needed [S]</item><item>Continue the care plan agreed on 1897-04-06 [S]</item><item>Next visit 1897-08-17: three-month sleepiness and headache review [S]</item></list></text>

